  "notes": "USAGE:\n{連合|れんごう} can function as both a noun and a する verb. As a noun, it refers to an alliance or union of entities. As a verb ({連合|れんごう}する), it means to unite or join forces.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {連合|れんごう}を{組|く}む (to form an alliance)\n- {連合|れんごう}を{結|むす}ぶ (to enter into an alliance)\n- {連合|れんごう}{軍|ぐん} (allied forces)\n- {連合|れんごう}{国|こく} (United Nations)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n{連合|れんごう}{国|こく} is the Japanese term for the United Nations. {連合|れんごう}{軍|ぐん} refers to allied forces, commonly used when discussing World War II history.",
